codex
The central version race is behaving safely: old-version passes stop counting if the head changes, and SQLite serializes the final status change against a competing version update. The weak points are elsewhere—zero-floor jobs, roster shrinkage, and reviewer-thread failures that are not durably recorded. I’m validating those paths now, including the live database settings and migration behavior.
